<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Shared test settings for the IP Intelligence example test projects.

  The on-premise integration tests each build a real engine against the
  enterprise IP Intelligence data file, which is several gigabytes. Running
  more than one of those at a time (the default MSTest behaviour is to
  parallelize across CPU cores) loads several multi-GB engines into memory
  simultaneously, which exhausts RAM on CI runners and causes the job to time
  out. These settings force the heavy on-premise tests to run one at a time and
  bound the overall runtime so a stuck test fails cleanly instead of hanging the
  runner.

  Referenced from each test project's <RunSettingsFilePath>, so it applies to
  MSBuild-driven runs - `dotnet test` against a project or the solution, and the
  IDE test runners.

  It does NOT currently apply in CI. ci/run-unit-tests.ps1 selects built
  assemblies by name, so common-ci invokes `dotnet test` against an assembly
  path with the no-build switch. That bypasses MSBuild, which is what would
  otherwise turn <RunSettingsFilePath> into a settings argument, so none of the
  settings below are in force there. The only per-test ceiling on CI is vstest's
  blame hang timeout, set and explained in ci/run-unit-tests.ps1. Treat the
  timeouts below as local/IDE guards until that wiring is fixed.

  (Keep this comment free of double hyphens: they are not legal inside an XML
  comment, and a malformed file here breaks every MSBuild-driven test run.)
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <!-- Whole-session ceiling (ms) so a local or IDE run cannot hang
         indefinitely. Must comfortably exceed the serial runtime of the
         on-premise suite on a slow, cold machine. On CI nothing bounds the
         session but the job timeout; see the note above. -->
    <TestSessionTimeout>1200000</TestSessionTimeout>
  </RunConfiguration>
  <MSTest>
    <!-- Per-test ceiling (ms). Deliberately generous: the Metadata example
         loads the multi-GB enterprise data file and enumerates every property
         and value, which has been observed to take over four minutes on a cold
         macOS CI runner. A tighter limit false-fails that legitimately slow
         test. True hangs are bounded here for local and IDE runs, and on CI by
         the blame hang timeout in ci/run-unit-tests.ps1. -->
    <TestTimeout>600000</TestTimeout>
    <!-- Belt and braces for running tests serially, so that only one multi-GB
         engine is loaded at a time. The actual guarantee comes from the
         [assembly: DoNotParallelize] in TestExamples.cs, which unlike this file
         does apply on CI.
         Concurrency itself is still covered by
         TestGettingStartedOnPremise.GettingStarted_ParallelProcessing_IsConsistent,
         which exercises many concurrent requests against a single shared engine. -->
    <Parallelize>
      <Workers>1</Workers>
      <Scope>ClassLevel</Scope>
    </Parallelize>
  </MSTest>
</RunSettings>
